      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I agree with this, your HARD CORE ROCK AND ROLE METAL BANGER group doesn't need to know that you attend Saturday morning knitting unless you want them to. You don't tell every \"group\" you join irl what other groups you hang out with do you. Some things random people just don't need to know. I think this is especially important for certain groups too, for example, lets say you have an Alcoholics Anonymous group in VRC, that might not be something you want just displayed on your profile. But is definitely the type of group that would probably be a public group based on its purpose alone.",
